<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:32:default:default">
<!--
    Arithmetic runtime helpers as C operators (`option arithhelpers on|off`,
    default on; stage P2 flow-classification, call-fixup injection).

    A 32-bit target delegates 64-bit division, modulo, multiplication and
    shifts, and on ARM every integer division, to a runtime helper: libgcc's
    __udivdi3 family, the ARM run-time ABI's __aeabi_uldivmod family, the MSVC
    CRT's __stdcall _alldiv family. Each helper is a synthesized <callfixup>
    whose p-code body is the operator, so the call prints as `a / b`.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture. Each group clears
    it and loads a real fixture from arithhelpers.c (sources and build lines
    beside the fixtures):
    - arithhelpers_i386: gcc -m32 ELF, libgcc linked in, DWARF-typed;
    - arithhelpers_thumb: clang Thumb-1 (ARMv6-M) ELF calling __aeabi_*;
    - arithhelpers_msvc_i386.exe: clang MSVC-ABI PE whose PDB names _alldiv.

    The first pass of each group (`option arithhelpers off`) reproduces the
    opaque helper calls; the second (the shipped default) prints operators.
    Assertions span the combined output of all passes.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
